lm832x: don't lose the first key event after configuration

READ_FIFO advances past the FIFO's first byte, the last event already
serviced (as the comment in the model shows the chip doing), and
returns nothing while only that byte is left. Configuring the chip
emptied the FIFO completely, so the first key event took the place of
that byte and was never returned: the first key press after boot was
lost and only its release reported. Start with an empty "last
serviced" byte instead.

diff --git a/hw/input/lm832x.c b/hw/input/lm832x.c
index 59e5567af..18fbd2dcf 100644
--- a/hw/input/lm832x.c
+++ b/hw/input/lm832x.c
@@ -268,7 +268,10 @@ static void lm_kbd_write(LM823KbdState *s, int reg, int byte, uint8_t value)
          * warnings.  */
         s->status = 0;
         lm_kbd_irq_update(s);
-        s->kbd.len = 0;
+        /* READ_FIFO returns the events after the one at the start, which
+         * is the last event serviced: none yet */
+        s->kbd.fifo[0] = 0x00;
+        s->kbd.len = 1;
         s->kbd.start = 0;
         s->reg = LM832x_GENERAL_ERROR;
         break;
